      "when_a_species_drops_below_10_of_its_c": "When a species drops below 10% of its carrying capacity (K), it has collapsed. Real-world example: Atlantic cod (1992 Newfoundland) collapsed from over-fishing and hasn't recovered 30+ years later. Sharks below 10% of K is also catastrophic because they're the top predator, and removing them cascades down the food web.",
