      "maine_roads_use_brine_rock_salt_all_wi": "Maine roads use brine + rock salt all winter. Salt + steel = rust within DAYS, not weeks. After every wet/slushy ride: rinse the bike with a hose, dry the chain, re-lube. Skip this and you'll go through chains and cassettes 3-4x faster than summer riders. Aluminum frames are mostly fine; steel frames need extra care, especially at welds.",
