      "most_octopuses_are_semelparous_they_re": "Most octopuses are semelparous — they reproduce ONCE and then die. The female brood her eggs continuously without eating until they hatch.",
      "most_octopuses_are_solitary_but_at_lea": "Most octopuses are SOLITARY, but at least 4 species are now documented as facultatively social — including Octopus tetricus in Jervis Bay, where 16+ individuals share a single artificial reef.",
      "most_octopuses_live_1_2_years_they_mat": "Most octopuses live 1-2 years. They mate once, brood eggs without eating, then die. Semelparous reproduction is the cephalopod default.",
