      "every_serious_shop_had_a_mark_called_a": "Every serious shop had a mark, called a \"device\" or colophon. It went on the title page and the last page. It signaled who printed the book, which mattered when (a) buyers wanted quality and (b) authorities wanted accountability. The dolphin-and-anchor was so successful Aldus Manutius spent half his career suing counterfeiters.",
